IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`

-- coa10-disclosure.l4: Chapter 11, ss 458 to 462 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): disclosure of information by the
-- tax authorities to a person authorised under s 457, that person's power to require documents, information and explanations,
-- and the restrictions on and exceptions to the disclosure of what is obtained. Lines 6220-6322 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is
-- within the rule; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`); NOTHING = the text does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- These sections mostly address officials; they are encoded for what they mean to the person asked for documents, the person
-- who holds information obtained under them, and the officer of a body that commits an offence under them.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 458: disclosure of information by tax authorities
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6221 | (1) The Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs may disclose information to a person authorised under section 457 for the purpose of facilitating—
-- src:6222 | (a) the taking of steps by that person to discover whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456 (application in respect of defective accounts etc), or
-- src:6223 | (b) a decision by the authorised person whether to make such an application.
-- src:6224 | (2) This section applies despite any statutory or other restriction on the disclosure of information.
-- src:6225 | Provided that, in the case of personal data within the meaning of Parts 5 to 7 of the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3(2) and (14) of that Act), information is not to be disclosed in contravention of the data protection legislation.
@ref s 458(1) HMRC may disclose information to a person authorised under section 457, but not in contravention of the data protection legislation (src:6221-6225)
GIVEN `the information is disclosed to a person authorised under section 457` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for the purpose of facilitating the taking of steps to discover whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456, or a decision whether to make such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is personal data within the meaning of Parts 5 to 7 of the Data Protection Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458(1) the Commissioners may disclose the information to the authorised person` MEANS
    IF `the information is personal data within the meaning of Parts 5 to 7 of the Data Protection Act 2018` AND `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of personal data within the meaning of Parts 5 to 7 of the Data Protection Act 2018 ..., information is not to be disclosed in contravention of the data protection legislation"
    ELSE IF `the information is disclosed to a person authorised under section 457` AND `the disclosure is for the purpose of facilitating the taking of steps to discover whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456, or a decision whether to make such an application`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may disclose information to a person authorised under section 457 for the purpose of facilitating"

-- (2): "This section applies despite any statutory or other restriction on the disclosure of information." Title as the bar.
-- src:6224 | (2) This section applies despite any statutory or other restriction on the disclosure of information.
@ref s 458(2) The section applies despite any statutory or other restriction on disclosure (src:6224)
GIVEN `a statutory or other restriction on the disclosure of information applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458(2) a statutory or other restriction bars the disclosure under this section` MEANS
    IF `a statutory or other restriction on the disclosure of information applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies despite any statutory or other restriction on the disclosure of information."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says only what the section does despite a restriction

-- (3): information disclosed to an authorised person may be used only in or in connection with steps to discover whether there
-- are grounds for an application to the court, deciding whether to make one, or proceedings on one; and not further disclosed
-- except to the person to whom it relates or in or in connection with such proceedings. Titled as the bar: JUST TRUE means barred.
DECLARE `s 458 use of the information` IS ONE OF
    `s 458 use in or in connection with taking steps to discover whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456`
    `s 458 use in or in connection with deciding whether or not to make such an application`
    `s 458 use in or in connection with proceedings on such an application`
    `s 458 any other use`

DECLARE `s 458 further disclosure of the information` IS ONE OF
    `s 458 disclosure to the person to whom the information relates`
    `s 458 disclosure in or in connection with proceedings on any such application to the court`
    `s 458 any other disclosure`

-- src:6226 | (3) Information disclosed to an authorised person under this section—
-- src:6227 | (a) may not be used except in or in connection with—
-- src:6228 | (i) taking steps to discover whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456, or
-- src:6229 | (ii) deciding whether or not to make such an application,
-- src:6230 | or in, or in connection with, proceedings on such an application; and
@ref s 458(3)(a) The information may not be used except in or in connection with the listed purposes (src:6226-6230)
GIVEN use IS A `s 458 use of the information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458(3)(a) the section bars the use of the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `s 458 any other use` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "except" met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "may not be used except in or in connection with— (i) taking steps to discover whether there are grounds ..., or (ii) deciding whether or not to make such an application, or in, or in connection with, proceedings on such an application"

-- src:6226 | (3) Information disclosed to an authorised person under this section—
-- src:6231 | (b) must not be further disclosed except—
-- src:6232 | (i) to the person to whom the information relates, or
-- src:6233 | (ii) in, or in connection with, proceedings on any such application to the court.
@ref s 458(3)(b) The information must not be further disclosed except to the person it relates to or in proceedings (src:6226 and src:6231-6233)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `s 458 further disclosure of the information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458(3)(b) the section bars the further disclosure of the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER disclosure
    WHEN `s 458 any other disclosure` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "except" met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "must not be further disclosed except— (i) to the person to whom the information relates, or (ii) in, or in connection with, proceedings on any such application to the court"

-- (4): a person who contravenes (3) commits an offence unless (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the
-- information had been disclosed under this section, or (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence.
-- The offence and its defences are the same sentence in s 460(4), which calls this function.
-- src:6234 | (4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits an offence unless—
-- src:6235 | (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under this section, or
-- src:6236 | (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence.
@ref s 458(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits an offence unless he did not know, or took all reasonable steps (src:6234-6236)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under the section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under the section` OR `he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "unless" met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "commits an offence unless— (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under this section, or (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person contravenes subsection (3)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who contravenes subsection (3)"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person contravenes subsection (3) is not known

-- (5): the penalties, by the way the person is convicted. The text distinguishes England and Wales from Scotland and Northern Ireland
-- on summary conviction; a summary conviction with no place named is not covered. "a fine (or both)" on indictment has no stated limit.
-- src:6237 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (4) is liable—
-- src:6238 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:6239 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:6240 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:6241 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 458(5) The penalties for the offence (src:6237-6241)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 458(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, (JUST (Period OF 2, Years)), (JUST `a fine without a stated limit`), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, (JUST (Period OF 12, Months)), (JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, (JUST (Period OF 6, Months)), (JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, (JUST (Period OF 6, Months)), (JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives different penalties for England and Wales and for Scotland or Northern Ireland and does not name a general summary conviction

-- (6): where a body corporate commits the offence, every officer of the body who is in default also commits it. The "in default"
-- answer is s 1121's (coa24), an INPUT. (a) and (b) say who is treated as an officer.
-- src:6243 | (a) any person who purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body is treated as an officer of the body, and
-- src:6244 | (b) if the body is a company, any shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 458(6) Who is treated as an officer of the body corporate (src:6243-6244)
GIVEN `the person purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company and the person is a shadow director of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458(6) the person is treated as an officer of the body` MEANS
    IF `the person purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body` OR `the body is a company and the person is a shadow director of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the paragraphs say who "is treated as an officer"; they do not say that no one else is

-- src:6242 | (6) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, every officer of the body who is in default also commits the offence. For this purpose—
@ref s 458(6) Where a body corporate commits the offence, every officer of the body who is in default also commits it (src:6242)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under the section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458(6) the officer of the body corporate also commits the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the body corporate commits an offence under the section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, every officer of the body who is in default also commits the offence"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person is an officer of the body corporate`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the body who is in default"
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is not known
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the body"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is not known

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 459: power of authorised person to require documents, information and explanations
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6247 | (1) This section applies where it appears to a person who is authorised under section 457 that there is, or may be, a question whether a company's annual accounts , strategic report or directors’ report complies comply with the requirements of this Act ....
@ref s 459(1) Where the section applies (src:6247)
GIVEN `it appears to a person who is authorised under section 457 that there is, or may be, a question whether a company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(1) section 459 applies` MEANS
    IF `it appears to a person who is authorised under section 457 that there is, or may be, a question whether a company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report comply with the requirements of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "This section applies where it appears to a person who is authorised under section 457 that there is, or may be, a question whether"

-- src:6251 | (3) Those persons are—
-- src:6252 | (a) the company;
-- src:6253 | (b) any officer, employee, or auditor of the company;
-- src:6254 | (c) any persons who fell within paragraph (b) at a time to which the document or information required by the authorised person relates.
@ref s 459(3) The persons who may be required (src:6251-6254)
DECLARE `s 459 kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 459 the company`
    `s 459 an officer, employee or auditor of the company`
    `s 459 a person who fell within the previous paragraph at a time to which the document or information required relates`
    `s 459 any other person`

-- src:6251 | (3) Those persons are—
-- src:6252 | (a) the company;
-- src:6253 | (b) any officer, employee, or auditor of the company;
-- src:6254 | (c) any persons who fell within paragraph (b) at a time to which the document or information required by the authorised person relates.
@ref s 459(3) Those persons are the company, its officers, employees and auditors, and former ones as to the relevant time (src:6251-6254)
GIVEN person IS A `s 459 kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(3) the person is one whom the authorised person may require` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `s 459 any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Those persons are— (a) the company; (b) ...; (c) ..." does not say "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6248 | (2) The authorised person may require any of the persons mentioned in subsection (3) to produce any document, or to provide him with any information or explanations, that he may reasonably require for the purpose of—
-- src:6249 | (a) discovering whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456, or
-- src:6250 | (b) deciding whether to make such an application.
@ref s 459(2) The authorised person may require documents, information or explanations (src:6248-6250)
GIVEN `s 459(1) section 459 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 459(3) the person is one whom the authorised person may require` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the authorised person reasonably requires the document, information or explanation for the purpose of discovering whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456, or deciding whether to make such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(2) the authorised person may require the person to produce the document or provide the information or explanation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 459(1) section 459 applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "This section applies where it appears to a person who is authorised under section 457"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT `the authorised person reasonably requires the document, information or explanation for the purpose of discovering whether there are grounds for an application to the court under section 456, or deciding whether to make such an application`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that he may reasonably require for the purpose of— (a) discovering whether there are grounds for an application ..., or (b) deciding whether to make such an application"
        ELSE `s 459(3) the person is one whom the authorised person may require`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known

-- src:6255 | (4) If a person fails to comply with such a requirement, the authorised person may apply to the court.
@ref s 459(4) If a person fails to comply with a requirement, the authorised person may apply to the court (src:6255)
GIVEN `the person has failed to comply with a requirement under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(4) the authorised person may apply to the court` MEANS
    IF `the person has failed to comply with a requirement under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person fails to comply with such a requirement, the authorised person may apply to the court."

-- src:6256 | (5) If it appears to the court that the person has failed to comply with a requirement under subsection (2), it may order the person to take such steps as it directs for securing that the documents are produced or the information or explanations are provided.
@ref s 459(5) The court may order the person to take steps where the requirement is not complied with (src:6256)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the person has failed to comply with a requirement under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(5) the court may order the person to take such steps as it directs` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court that the person has failed to comply with a requirement under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the court that the person has failed to comply with a requirement under subsection (2), it may order the person to take such steps as it directs"

-- src:6257 | (6) A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under subsection (2) or an order under subsection (5) may not be used in evidence against him in any criminal proceedings.
@ref s 459(6) A statement made in response may not be used in evidence against the maker in criminal proceedings (src:6257)
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement under subsection (2) or an order under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are criminal proceedings against the person who made the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(6) the statement may be used in evidence against the person who made it` MEANS
    IF `the statement was made in response to a requirement under subsection (2) or an order under subsection (5)` AND `the proceedings are criminal proceedings against the person who made the statement`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under subsection (2) or an order under subsection (5) may not be used in evidence against him in any criminal proceedings."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is of use "against him in any criminal proceedings"

-- src:6258 | (7) Nothing in this section compels any person to disclose documents or information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings.
@ref s 459(7) Nothing compels disclosure of what is legally privileged (src:6258)
GIVEN `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(7) the section compels the person to disclose the document or information` MEANS
    IF `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the document or information`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section compels any person to disclose documents or information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says only what the section does not compel

-- src:6259 | (8) In this section “document” includes information recorded in any form.
@ref s 459(8) "document" includes information recorded in any form (src:6259)
GIVEN `the thing is a document or information recorded in any form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459(8) the thing is a document for the purposes of section 459` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a document or information recorded in any form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section “document” includes information recorded in any form"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 460: restrictions on disclosure of information obtained under compulsory powers
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6261 | (1) This section applies to information (in whatever form) obtained in pursuance of a requirement or order under section 459 (power of authorised person to require documents etc) that relates to the private affairs of an individual or to any particular business.
@ref s 460(1) The information the section applies to (src:6261)
GIVEN `the information was obtained in pursuance of a requirement or order under section 459` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the private affairs of an individual or to any particular business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 460(1) the information is within section 460` MEANS
    IF `the information was obtained in pursuance of a requirement or order under section 459` AND `the information relates to the private affairs of an individual or to any particular business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to information (in whatever form) obtained in pursuance of a requirement or order under section 459 ... that relates to the private affairs of an individual or to any particular business"

-- (2), (3): no such information may, during the lifetime of the individual or so long as the business continues to be carried on,
-- be disclosed without the consent of that individual or the person then carrying on the business; (3): this does not apply to
-- disclosure permitted by s 461 or of information that is or has been available to the public from another source.
-- src:6262 | (2) No such information may, during the lifetime of that individual or so long as that business continues to be carried on, be disclosed without the consent of that individual or the person for the time being carrying on that business.
-- src:6263 | (3) This does not apply—
-- src:6264 | (a) to disclosure permitted by section 461 (permitted disclosure of information obtained under compulsory powers), or
-- src:6265 | (b) to the disclosure of information that is or has been available to the public from another source.
@ref s 460(2), (3) The section bars disclosure of the information without consent (src:6262-6265)
GIVEN `s 460(1) the information is within section 460` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is alive, or the business continues to be carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual, or the person for the time being carrying on the business, has consented to the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is permitted by section 461` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information is or has been available to the public from another source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 460(2) the section bars the disclosure of the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 460(1) the information is within section 460`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies only to the information subsection (1) describes
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies only to the information subsection (1) describes
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the information is or has been available to the public from another source`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply— ... (b) to the disclosure of information that is or has been available to the public from another source."
        ELSE IF `the disclosure is permitted by section 461` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply— (a) to disclosure permitted by section 461"
             ELSE IF NOT `the individual is alive, or the business continues to be carried on`
                  THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the lifetime of that individual or so long as that business continues to be carried on"
                  ELSE IF `the individual, or the person for the time being carrying on the business, has consented to the disclosure`
                       THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of that individual or the person for the time being carrying on that business"
                       ELSE CONSIDER `the disclosure is permitted by section 461`
                            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
                            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the disclosure is permitted by section 461 is not known

-- src:6266 | (4) A person who discloses information in contravention of this section commits an offence, unless—
-- src:6267 | (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under section 459, or
-- src:6268 | (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence.
@ref s 460(4) A person who discloses in contravention commits an offence unless he did not know, or took all reasonable steps (src:6266-6268)
GIVEN `the person discloses information in contravention of section 460` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under section 459` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 460(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under section 459` OR `he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "unless" met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "commits an offence, unless— (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been disclosed under section 459, or (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person discloses information in contravention of section 460`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who discloses information in contravention of this section"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the disclosure contravenes the section is not known

-- (5): the penalties are those of s 458(5), word for word; (6): the officer-in-default sentence is s 458(6)'s, word for word.
-- src:6269 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:6270 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:6271 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:6272 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:6273 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 460(5) The penalties for the offence (src:6269-6273)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 460(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    `s 458(5) the penalty for the offence` `how the person is convicted`

-- src:6275 | (a) any person who purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body is treated as an officer of the body, and
-- src:6276 | (b) if the body is a company, any shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 460(6) Who is treated as an officer of the body corporate (src:6275-6276)
GIVEN `the person purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company and the person is a shadow director of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 460(6) the person is treated as an officer of the body` MEANS
    `s 458(6) the person is treated as an officer of the body` `the person purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body` `the body is a company and the person is a shadow director of it`

-- src:6274 | (6) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, every officer of the body who is in default also commits the offence. For this purpose—
@ref s 460(6) Where a body corporate commits the offence, every officer of the body who is in default also commits it (src:6274)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under the section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 460(6) the officer of the body corporate also commits the offence` MEANS
    `s 458(6) the officer of the body corporate also commits the offence` `the body corporate commits an offence under the section` `the person is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 461: permitted disclosure of information obtained under compulsory powers
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The exceptions to the prohibition in s 460, by whom the information goes to and for what purpose. The text lists the
-- recipients in (3), the purposes in (4) and a class of overseas bodies in (5); it says "does not apply", so each listed case
-- is JUST TRUE; a case in none of the lists is NOTHING (the lists are not closed with "only"), except that (7) says no.

DECLARE `s 461 recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 461 the Secretary of State`
    `s 461 the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment for Northern Ireland`
    `s 461 the Treasury`
    `s 461 the Bank of England`
    `s 461 the Financial Conduct Authority`
    `s 461 the Prudential Regulation Authority`
    `s 461 the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    `s 461 a body exercising functions of a public nature under legislation in a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
    `s 461 any other recipient`

-- src:6279 | (2) It does not apply to the disclosure of information for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the authorised person of his functions under section 456.
@ref s 461(2) Disclosure for the purpose of facilitating the authorised person's functions under section 456 (src:6279)
GIVEN `the disclosure is for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the authorised person of his functions under section 456` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(2) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the authorised person of his functions under section 456`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (2) names one purpose and does not say "only"

-- src:6280 | (3) It does not apply to disclosure to—
-- src:6281 | (a) the Secretary of State,
-- src:6282 | (b) the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment for Northern Ireland,
-- src:6283 | (c) the Treasury,
-- src:6284 | (d) the Bank of England,
-- src:6285 | (e) the Financial Conduct Authority,
-- src:6286 | (ea) the Prudential Regulation Authority, or
-- src:6287 | (f) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs.
@ref s 461(3) Disclosure to the Secretary of State, the Northern Ireland Department, the Treasury, the Bank of England, the FCA, the PRA or HMRC (src:6280-6287)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 461 recipient`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(3) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure to the recipient` MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `s 461 any other recipient` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (3) lists seven public authorities and does not say "only"
    WHEN `s 461 a body exercising functions of a public nature under legislation in a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): such a body is subsection (5)'s case, not subsection (3)'s
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the purposes for which disclosure is permitted.
DECLARE `s 461 purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 461 assisting the Financial Reporting Council Limited to exercise its functions under Part 42 of the Act`
    `s 461 assisting the competent authority to exercise its functions under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 and under the Audit Regulation`
    `s 461 disciplinary proceedings relating to the performance by an accountant or auditor of his professional duties`
    `s 461 enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under the Companies Acts, Part 5 of the Criminal Justice Act 1993, the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989, the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002, or the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
    `s 461 enabling or assisting the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment for Northern Ireland to exercise any powers conferred on it by the enactments relating to companies, directors' disqualification or insolvency`
    `s 461 enabling or assisting the Bank of England to exercise its functions`
    `s 461 enabling or assisting the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs to exercise their functions`
    `s 461 enabling or assisting the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority to exercise its functions under the legislation relating to friendly societies, the Credit Unions Act 1979, the Building Societies Act 1986, Part 7 of the Companies Act 1989, the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 or the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014`
    `s 461 in pursuance of any assimilated obligation`
    `s 461 any other purpose`

-- src:6288 | (4) It does not apply to disclosure—
-- src:6289 | (a) for the purpose of assisting the Financial Reporting Council Limited to exercise it functions under Part 42 of this Act;
-- src:6290 | (aa) for the purpose of assisting the competent authority to exercise its functions under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 and under the Audit Regulation;
-- src:6291 | (b) with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, disciplinary proceedings relating to the performance by an accountant or auditor of his professional duties;
-- src:6292 | (c) for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Secretary of State or the Treasury to exercise any of their functions under any of the following—
-- src:6293 | (i) the Companies Acts,
-- src:6294 | (ii) Part 5 of the Criminal Justice Act 1993 (c. 36) (insider dealing),
-- src:6295 | (iii) the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)),
-- src:6296 | (iv) the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (c. 46) or the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (S.I. 2002/3150 (N.I. 4)),
-- src:6297 | (v) the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8);
-- src:6298 | (d) for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Investment for Northern Ireland to exercise any powers conferred on it by the enactments relating to companies, directors' disqualification or insolvency;
-- src:6299 | (e) for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Bank of England to exercise its functions;
-- src:6300 | (f) for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs to exercise their functions;
-- src:6301 | (g) for the purpose of enabling or assisting the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority to exercise its functions under any of the following—
-- src:6302 | (i) the legislation relating to friendly societies ...,
-- src:6303 | (ia) the Credit Unions Act 1979,
-- src:6304 | (ii) the Building Societies Act 1986 (c. 53),
-- src:6305 | (iii) Part 7 of the Companies Act 1989 (c. 40),
-- src:6306 | (iv) the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000;
-- src:6307 | (v) the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014; or
-- src:6308 | (h) in pursuance of any assimilated obligation.
@ref s 461(4) Disclosure for the listed purposes (src:6288-6308)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 461 purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(4) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure for the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 461 any other purpose` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (4) lists purposes and does not say "only"; section 462 gives the Secretary of State power to add more
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (5), (6): disclosure to an overseas body exercising similar functions, with the considerations the authorised person must have regard to.
-- src:6309 | (5) It does not apply to disclosure to a body exercising functions of a public nature under legislation in any country or territory outside the United Kingdom that appear to the authorised person to be similar to his functions under section 456 for the purpose of enabling or assisting that body to exercise those functions.
@ref s 461(5) Disclosure to an overseas body exercising similar functions (src:6309)
GIVEN `the body exercises functions of a public nature under legislation in a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those functions appear to the authorised person to be similar to his functions under section 456` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for the purpose of enabling or assisting that body to exercise those functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(5) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure to the overseas body` MEANS
    IF `the body exercises functions of a public nature under legislation in a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
       AND `those functions appear to the authorised person to be similar to his functions under section 456`
       AND `the disclosure is for the purpose of enabling or assisting that body to exercise those functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a body exercising functions of a public nature under legislation in any country or territory outside the United Kingdom that appear to the authorised person to be similar to his functions under section 456 for the purpose of enabling or assisting that body to exercise those functions"

-- src:6310 | (6) In determining whether to disclose information to a body in accordance with subsection (5), the authorised person must have regard to the following considerations—
-- src:6311 | (a) whether the use which the body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure;
-- src:6312 | (b) whether the body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed other than—
-- src:6313 | (i) for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in that subsection, or
-- src:6314 | (ii) for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the authorised person could be used or further disclosed.
@ref s 461(6) In determining whether to disclose to an overseas body the authorised person must have regard to two considerations (src:6310-6314)
GIVEN `the authorised person has had regard to whether the use which the body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised person has had regard to whether the body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(6) the authorised person has had regard to the considerations the section names` MEANS
    IF `the authorised person has had regard to whether the use which the body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure`
       AND `the authorised person has had regard to whether the body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes the paragraph names`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not done, decided at this site, ruling of 2026-11-05): "the authorised person must have regard to the following considerations"

-- (7): "Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation."
-- src:6315 | (7) Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation.
@ref s 461(7) Nothing in the section authorises a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation (src:6315)
GIVEN `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(7) the section authorises the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says only what the section does not authorise

-- src:6278 | (1) The prohibition in section 460 of the disclosure of information obtained in pursuance of a requirement or order under section 459 (power of authorised person to require documents etc) that relates to the private affairs of an individual or to any particular business has effect subject to the following exceptions.
@ref s 461(1) The prohibition in section 460 has effect subject to the exceptions in section 461 (src:6278)
GIVEN `s 461(2) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to the disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 461(3) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure to the recipient` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 461(4) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure for the purpose` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 461(5) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure to the overseas body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 461(7) the section authorises the disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(1) the disclosure is permitted by section 461` MEANS
    IF `s 461(7) the section authorises the disclosure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation."
    ELSE IF    `s 461(2) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to the disclosure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `s 461(3) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure to the recipient` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `s 461(4) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure for the purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `s 461(5) the prohibition in section 460 does not apply to disclosure to the overseas body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the exceptions in subsections (2) to (5) are not said to be the only ones, and section 462 lets the Secretary of State amend them
